# "Whenever you cast a spell that targets a creature you control" is not only about Ms. Marvel herself: Bot1 casts Snakeskin
# Veil at its Ornithopter on turn 3. The Ornithopter gets the counter, but it is Ms. Marvel who draws (the controller does) and
# who gains the static ability: her base power is the two cards left in Bot1's hand, not the Ornithopter's.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Ornithopter
Ms. Marvel, Kamala Khan
Mox Emerald
Snakeskin Veil
Island
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ms. Marvel, Kamala Khan.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Snakeskin Veil.Cast(Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ms. Marvel, Kamala Khan.Power = 2
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 0
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ms. Marvel, Kamala Khan.Power = 2
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 1

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand.Count = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Ms. Marvel, Kamala Khan.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
